    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0547" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg467"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-11-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 21, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 431.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 418 of the
                    27th ultimo, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of a note which I have
                    received from the Marquis of Lansdowne in relation to the American prisoners of
                    war in Ceylon, together with a copy of a telegram<anchor n="a" xml:id="d456-f1"
                    /> which I sent you on the 21st instant, from which it will be observed that the
                    American consul at Colombo can communicate with the 22 prisoners of war, but
                    that all communications should be made either through the governor of Ceylon or
                    through the general officer commanding the troops.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d456-a1.xml" xpointer="d456-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
